    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0545" n="513" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v18/pg513"/>

                <head>250. Memorandum From the President’s Special Assistant for National Security
                    Affairs (Bundy) and Robert W. Komer of the
                    National Security Council Staff to President Johnson<anchor n="1" xml:id="d250-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1965-11-08">November 8, 1965</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Food for the UAR</hi>.
                        Rusk’s new package<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d250-f2"/> seems to meet the criteria you gave him at the
                        ranch.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d250-f3"/> In fact, it is tough enough that
                        Nasser may insist on arguing about
                    it, even though our Embassy says he’s by now almost desperate enough to grasp at
                    any straw.</p>
                <p>It is also tough enough (far less than the UAR
                    asked, or than we’ve previously given) to be politically defensible here. If it
                    works, we can point to the lower quantities, tougher terms, dollar returns, and
                    rice for Vietnam.</p>
                <p>Since State/AID now seem to be talking the right tune, we recommend you go ahead.
                    It’s possible to design an even tougher package (e.g. six months’ instead of a
                    year) but doubt that we could hang on it such conditions as free rice for
                        Vietnam.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d250-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">
                            R. W. Komer
                        </hi>
                        <lb/> McGB.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d250-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d250-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, Country File, United Arab
                    Republic, Vol. IV. Secret. Received at the LBJ
                    Ranch on November 9 at 5 p.m.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d250-f2" n="2" xml:id="d250-f2-content">
                <p>An attached memorandum of November 8 from Rusk to the President recommended a P.L. 480 package totaling $109.5 million for the UAR.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d250-f3" n="3" xml:id="d250-f3-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d247">Document 247</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d250-f4" n="4" xml:id="d250-f4-content">
                <p>Johnson wrote at the bottom of the memorandum: “I want to talk to Rusk &amp; Bundy about this
                    Thursday. L.” Thursday was November 11.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
